1. Product Overview
This document outlines the plan to build and sell an AI-powered educational app that helps school and college students study more effectively. Students upload any textbook chapter, PDF, or handwritten notes, and the app instantly generates practice questions, model answers, and a performance scorecard.

1.1 Core Features
•	Document upload: PDF, scanned textbook pages, typed notes
•	AI question generation: MCQ, true/false, short answer, fill-in-the-blank
•	Model answers with step-by-step explanations
•	Timed quiz mode and open practice mode
•	Performance scorecard: score, weak topics, improvement trends
•	Retake system that focuses on areas the student got wrong
•	Student dashboard with subject-wise progress tracking

1.2 How It Works
The app is powered by the Claude AI API (Anthropic). When a student uploads a document, the text is extracted and sent to Claude with a structured prompt. Claude returns a set of questions and answers, which are displayed in the app. After the student completes the quiz, results are saved and the scorecard is generated automatically.
No custom AI training is required. The product is built on top of existing AI infrastructure, which dramatically reduces development cost and time.

